%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0ca23d3e41cd5424c9ec72c610ef25a4, type: 3}
  m_Name: LeavesGramorTomb
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  autoFocusSpeaker: 1
  screens:
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598929
    - rid: 1790118583906598931
    - rid: 1790118583906598932
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Haaaahh...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598933
    - rid: 1790118583906598934
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: That feels nice-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598935
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: The constant tinge of bloodlust was actually pretty heavy.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598936
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Are my wolf ears gone?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598937
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 6f47b2f061a0a3249992cdd21d6995ed, type: 2}
    dialog: Ah... no.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598938
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Dang it!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598939
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Guess I gotta go to that face-sculptor or whatever...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598940
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 6f47b2f061a0a3249992cdd21d6995ed, type: 2}
    dialog: If we've got no more business here, we should head back to the others.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598941
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Yeah, yeah.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598942
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598943
    - rid: 1790118583906598944
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: You're back, is it done? Has Kodlak's soul been freed from Hircine?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598946
    - rid: 1790118583906598947
    - rid: 1790118583906598948
    - rid: 1790118583906598949
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Yep. My soul's been cleansed too-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598950
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Even <i>if</i> you couldn't tell because of these dang ears!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598951
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: I see. My apologies.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598952
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 6f47b2f061a0a3249992cdd21d6995ed, type: 2}
    dialog: Vilkas.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: Yes?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 6f47b2f061a0a3249992cdd21d6995ed, type: 2}
    dialog: The old man named you Natsuki's Harbinger-Regent.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598953
    - rid: 1790118583906598954
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: I- that's...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: Very peculiar.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 17bd3b6fcae930647918fc183fea836b, type: 2}
    dialog: I know Kodlak was the old Harbinger, but what's a Harbinger-Regent?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598956
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: (That's what I'm sayin'!)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: The title of Harbinger-Regent is fairly obscure; there's only been barely
      a dozen of them in the over thousand-year history of the Companions.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598957
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: The first recorded instance of a Harbinger-Regent came from the Second
      Era...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: When Aldar Stormaxe, who was Harbinger at the time, was on his death
      bed, there wasn't a single honorable warrior he could trust to pass on the
      title.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: Not to imply that no one had honor whatsoever, merely that he couldn't
      trust any of them to be the impartial arbiters that being Harbinger requires.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: 'There were only two people he considered potentially worthy: an Argonian
      named Throws-his-Shield and a young Nord named Svana Icebrow.'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: Aldar had been grooming Svana as his protege, which meant he trusted
      her potential, but she was too young to be Harbinger.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: Throws-his-Shield was a capable and wise warrior, but the warriors at
      that time wouldn't have accepted an Argonian Harbinger.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: Which is why Aldar declared that Throws-his-Shield would be Svana's Harbinger-Regent-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: He would serve as her direct counsel, trainer, and teacher until the
      Circle voted to officiate Svana as the Harbinger.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: In this way, Throws-his-Shield's wisdom could influence the Companions
      without upsetting the other warriors by giving an Argonian the title.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: ... That doesn't explain why Kodlak didn't just make you the Harbinger.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598958
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: I don't know that for sure either-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598959
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: What I <i>do</i> know, is that you've managed to rise through our ranks
      and display great honor in just a few days.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598960
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: Undoubtedly, you have potential for great things; potential that hasn't
      been realized yet.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: I guess Kodlak would rather have a wiser Natsuki become Harbinger down
      the line than have me do it.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598966
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: 'Well then, for my first act as Soon-to-be-Harbinger:'
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598961
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Let's go rest at the inn in Winterhold; I'm pooped.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598962
    - rid: 1790118583906598967
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 17bd3b6fcae930647918fc183fea836b, type: 2}
    dialog: Looks like she won't be needing your wisdom that badly, brother.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598963
    - rid: 1790118583906598965
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 6f47b2f061a0a3249992cdd21d6995ed, type: 2}
    dialog: As if you need wisdom to suggest a break when you're tired-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: No, no, knowing when to stop, rest, and recover, and when to push your
      advantage is an important distinction.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: One that <i>you</i> could work on.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598968
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Farkas, you still got paper?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598969
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 17bd3b6fcae930647918fc183fea836b, type: 2}
    dialog: Yep. You writing down this word wall too?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598970
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: That's right.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 6f47b2f061a0a3249992cdd21d6995ed, type: 2}
    dialog: This one too? Have you written down the contents of other word walls?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598972
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Yuh-huh.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 6f47b2f061a0a3249992cdd21d6995ed, type: 2}
    dialog: Why? You could just leave them to the ice-brained scholars.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: A friend asked me to write them down whenever I find one.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 6f47b2f061a0a3249992cdd21d6995ed, type: 2}
    dialog: I see...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 639d4037fbc3acd41947392e6542aac6, type: 2}
    dialog: Natsuki finishes writing down the contents of the word wall onto the
      paper Farkas gave her.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598973
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Alright, now the inn.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598978
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: (Now that I'm thinking about it...)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118583906598974
    - rid: 1790118583906598975
    - rid: 1790118583906598976
    - rid: 1790118583906598977
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: (I didn't give {mc} the word wall I found at Dustman's Cairn, did I?)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions: []
